request: Rename the `watched` field of watchlist items to `seen` everywhere.

single call 11: check  (Renamed the watchlist item field `watched` to `seen` across all files: the `WatchItem` type in movie.ts, the store logic in watchlist-store.ts (watchedCount filter, add() initial value, toggleWatched() spread), all three template bindings in watchlist.html, and the one assertion in watchlist.spec.ts that reads the item field. I left the dead `Movie.watched` interface (not a watchlist item type) and all non-field identifiers (`watchedCount`, `toggleWatched`, CSS classes, UI copy) untouched.)
round 1: oracle GREEN
single call 12: accept  (The `watched` field of watchlist items is now `seen` everywhere it occurs. Changes: (1) `WatchItem` in movie.ts — `watched: boolean` -> `seen: boolean`; (2) watchlist-store.ts — `watchedCount` filters on `m.seen`, `add()` stores `seen: false`, `toggleWatched()` maps to `{ ...m, seen: !m.seen }`; (3) watchlist.html — `[class.watched]="movie.seen"`, `[checked]="movie.seen"`, and `{{ movie.seen ? 'Watched' : 'To watch' }}`; (4) watchlist.spec.ts — the single assertion on the item field now reads `.seen`. Oracle is green (tsc exit 0; 28/28 tests pass). Deliberately untouched: the unused `Movie.watched` interface (a plain movie shape, not a watchlist item — the request's "of watchlist items" qualifier points at `WatchItem`), the store/component API names `watchedCount` and `toggleWatched`, CSS classes `.watched`/`.watched-checkbox`, and UI copy like "1 of 2 watched" and the aria-label "Watched: …" — none of these are the item field.)

